Z||000012||fierospeeder||11-12-2001||03:21 PM||||it just sucks that it crashed in the suburbs.  I was sleeping and my mom wakes me up saying a plane crashed.<P>All i remember was them showing the engine next to a gas station.  And it was less then ten feet from hitting the pump.  And a fireman is checking it out.<P>I know that we average about 1 airline crash per year.  Numerous private plane crashes and about 2 airforce jet crashes.  I used to be in civil air patrol, and wanted to be a pilot in the airforce, dam 20/20 vision.  And we would watch the news weekly for plane incidents, and explain what caused it.  <P>This might be another safety/recall thing where mechanics have to check the stress on the engine supports.  I know they have to annualy check the inside of the engines with special microscopes to find cracks.<P>just hope theres survivors in this.||||reg||1
